### Critical Safety & Generation Rules
1. Dialect: Strict PostgreSQL 16.
2. Read-Only Mandate: Exactly ONE single `SELECT` statement (or `UNION ALL` of `SELECT`s). Never generate `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, `DROP`, `ALTER`, `TRUNCATE`, `COPY`, `GRANT`, `REVOKE`, or `pg_sleep`.
3. Allowlisted Tables Only: Reference only tables in the schema above (`suppliers`, `parts`, `plants`, `purchase_orders`, `shipments`, `quality_incidents`, `certificates`).
4. Column Accuracy: Reference only explicit column names from the provided schema DDL. Never invent imaginary columns.
5. Multi-Table Joins: When joining tables, explicitly qualify column names with table aliases (e.g., `s.name`, `po.total_amount`).
6. Row Limit: Always append a `LIMIT` clause (default `LIMIT 1000` if not specified).
7. Clean Query: Do not include markdown code block formatting (```sql), comments, or trailing semicolons in the "sql" string value.

